    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (**68 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**).\n\n## What I did\n\nI unified `customerCode`, `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (e.g. `NSW277D0C08EF9`).\n\n**New / renamed logic**\n- **`MemberIds`** (replaces `CustomerCodes`) \u2014 builds `memberId` = region (postcode\u2192city) + 2-digit fiscal year + the 8 upper-hex `HASH8` (`SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`, same as the region-and-hash identity) + a single Luhn `CHK` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Retains `hash8`, `deduplicate` (now on `memberId`), and `localityOf`.\n- **`AssignMemberId`** (replaces `AssignCustomerCode`) \u2014 assigns the deduplicated `memberId`; collision handling now applies to `memberId`. Deleted `AssignMembershipNumber` (its FY is now the `FY` segment).\n- **`CheckDigits`** \u2014 kept as the Luhn util (now feeds the `CHK` segment); javadoc updated.\n\n**Field/model/schema removals**\n- `Owner` \u2014 dropped `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields, added `memberId` (`member_id` column).\n- All four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 replaced the two columns with `member_id`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`; added `memberId`.\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 removed the `checkDigit` mapping, switched `locality` to `MemberIds`; `memberId` auto-maps by name.\n\n**Behaviour references retargeted to `memberId`**\n- `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 human-readable line now logs `memberId` (plus id, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` \u2014 structured event now carries the `memberId` under a `memberId` key.\n- `OwnerSegments` / `Timezones` \u2014 locality now via `MemberIds.localityOf`.\n- POST pipeline YAML rewired `build \u2192 assignMemberId \u2192 assignHousehold`.\n\nThe `fiscalYear` (`FY<YY>`) field remains, and its 2-digit year matches the `FY` segment embedded in `memberId`.",
